    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d788-a3">

                <pb facs="0876" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg682"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Attachment 3]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d788-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Political
                        Adviser to the Representative on the European Advisory Commission</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mosely</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-28">28 July [19]45</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Mosely secret from Winant, signed Tindall.</p>
                <p>Ref mytel for Mosely July 27 sent Dept as 7588 <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Comea</hi> 344,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d788-f2"/> following is text proposed
                    joint statement re consultation other Allied Govts for publication four capitals
                    upon four govts approval: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Title: Statement by Govts of US, UK and USSR and Provisional Govt French
                            Republic on consultation with other United Nations Govts.</p>
                        <p>Begin Text: In a statement issued on June 5, 1945<anchor n="4"
                                xml:id="d788-f3"/> the Govts of US, UK and USSR and Provisional Govt
                            French Republic announced their intention to consult the Govts of other
                            United Nations in connection with the exercise of supreme authority in
                            respect to Germany assumed by declaration re defeat of Germany signed at
                            Berlin June 5, 1945.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d788-f4"/> The Govts of the
                            four powers hereby announce that it is also their intention to consult
                            the Govts of the United Nations in connection with the exercise of this
                            authority in Austria. End Text.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d788-f5"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d788-f1" n="2" xml:id="d788-f1-content">
                <p>Not attached; printed from the file copy (file No. 740.00119 Control
                    (Germany)/7–2845). Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d788-f2" n="3" xml:id="d788-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d786">Document No. 786</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d788-f3" n="4" xml:id="d788-f3-content">
                <p>See Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">xii</hi>, p. 1053.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d788-f4" n="5" xml:id="d788-f4-content">
                <p>Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1520; 60 Stat. (2) 1649.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d788-f5" n="6" xml:id="d788-f5-content">
                <p>Although this draft statement was approved by Byrnes (see <ref target="#d789"
                        >document No. 789</ref>), it appears that it was never issued.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
